-- the same as a tree of steps, directly: the process interpreted at the type of steps, each
-- command's handler run at it too. to-step (linux-run pf le p) is this up to moving the
-- drivers' interpretation into the branches of every case on a response; here it is there from
-- the start, a step is data, and the specialized code has no function chosen at run time
linux-step : {A : Type} → (pf : Platform) → LittleEndian pf → Proc {lzero} Linux A → Step W A
linux-step {A} pf le p =
  scmd (w-alloc lx-scratch) (λ sc → p (Step W A) (λ a → sdone a) (λ c k → linux-on-w pf le sc c (Step W A) k (λ c2 k2 → scmd c2 k2)))
